      "literalSourceFidelity": true,
      "payloadCharacters": 5158,
      "configuredModel": "gpt-5.5",
      "status": "generated",
      "answer": "Rally Scoring means a team can win a point whether it is serving or receiving, except the game-winning point must be scored while serving.\n\nKey mechanics:\n- If the serving team loses a rally, it is a side out: the other team gets a point and takes the serve.\n- After a side out, the first server is based on that team’s score: right side serves if the score is even; left side serves if odd.\n- Players switch sides only after winning a point on their own serve, and the same player keeps serving from the new side.\n- A scoring freeze starts when a team reaches one point below the game-winning score. That team can score the winning point only while serving; the other team keeps normal rally scoring until it also reaches its freeze point.\n- In win-by-two games, if the score ties at or beyond the initial freeze point, both teams become unfrozen and normal rally scoring resumes. The freeze/unfreeze process continues as needed, and the game-winning point must always be scored while serving.",
