      "payloadCharacters": 5177,
      "configuredModel": "gpt-5.5",
      "status": "generated",
      "answer": "In a Picklebreaker using Rally Scoring:\n\n- A team can win a point whether it is serving or receiving, except for the game-winning point.\n- If the serving team loses a rally, it is a side out: the receiving team gets a point and takes over serve.\n- After a side out, the first server is based on that team’s score: right side serves on an even score, left side serves on an odd score.\n- Players switch sides only after winning a point on their own serve; the same player continues serving from the new side.\n- Scoring freezes when a team reaches one point below the game-winning score. Once frozen, that team can score the game-winning point only while serving.\n- The freeze applies only to the team that reached the freeze point; the other team continues normal Rally Scoring until it also reaches its freeze point.\n- In a win-by-two format, if the score becomes tied at or beyond the initial freeze point, both teams become unfrozen and normal Rally Scoring resumes. Scores freeze again whenever a team reaches a score where its next point would win by two. This freeze/unfreeze process continues until one team wins by two.\n\nThe game-winning point must always be scored while serving.",
